{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned22", "translation": "I double the word"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned23", "translation": "I double"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned24", "translation": "again"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned25", "translation": "word"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned26", "translation": "I double again"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned27", "translation": "revering well"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned28", "translation": "revering well"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned29", "translation": "to revere someone"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned30", "translation": "to revere"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned31", "translation": "to revere"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned32", "translation": "revering well"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-mentioned33", "translation": "honoring well"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-3-quote1", "translation": "to act impiously toward someone"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-4-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: see on 897; ⟦2⟧ litotes equivalent to ⟦3⟧; cf. 596, ⟦4⟧. 774 etc."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-4-mentioned1", "translation": "misfortunes"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-4-mentioned2", "translation": "you will not blame"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-371-4-mentioned3", "translation": "you will praise"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-1-comment1", "translation": "1021 ⟦1⟧ as ⟦2⟧ 922;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-1-mentioned1", "translation": "of prayers"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-1-mentioned2", "translation": "I pray"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ as ⟦2⟧. ⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧. ⟦5⟧ is not said (nor is ⟦6⟧ to be construed thus), but ⟦7⟧, which I restore. That Athena sends her own temple attendants along is a special honor; they must, however, be identical with a part of those named at 1025 ff., whom Athena designates as ⟦8⟧, i.e., as the flower, the most precious thing of the whole Attic land. Cf. ⟦9⟧ ⟦10⟧ ⟦11⟧⟦12⟧ ⟦13⟧⟦14⟧ (Amphiaraus), ⟦15⟧ 2, 11. (⟦16⟧ on 402. 689). There was a priestess of Athena and beside her a ⟦17⟧ and a ⟦18⟧ (Harpocr. ⟦19⟧, Wecklein)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned1", "translation": "of torch-bearing lights"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned2", "translation": "l"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned3", "translation": "light-bearing"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned4", "translation": "below the earth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned5", "translation": "down under the earth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned6", "translation": "eye of all the land of Theseus"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned7", "translation": "eye of the house"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned8", "translation": "eye of Sicily"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned9", "translation": "of Theseus"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned10", "translation": "table-bearer"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned11", "translation": "I adorn"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-mentioned12", "translation": "table-bearer"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-quote1", "translation": "eye of the house"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-2-quote2", "translation": "eye of my army"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ duly (Blaydes). ⟦2⟧ means 'to reach the goal' (⟦3⟧. 303, ⟦4⟧. 810), but the optative with ⟦5⟧ can be a request, as at Choeph. 105 ⟦6⟧; so Athena bids the ⟦7⟧ (1005), already visible to her before, now come fully forward."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-3-mentioned1", "translation": "justly"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-3-mentioned2", "translation": "to arrive"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-3-mentioned3", "translation": "then"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-3-mentioned4", "translation": "you might say"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-3-mentioned5", "translation": "escorts"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-4-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ as at 46;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-4-mentioned1", "translation": "company"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-5-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ 856."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-5-mentioned1", "translation": "procession"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-6-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ will be feminine (69, ⟦2⟧);"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-372-6-mentioned1", "translation": "of children"}]}